WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.868
-It was a busy day.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.434
Robert Mueller,
the former special counsel

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:06.868
in the Russia investigation,
testified before Congress today.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:09.334
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:11.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.868
Of course, Mueller's testimony
was highly anticipated

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.767
with lots of people
expected to watch,

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:20.434
except one guy who claimed
he wouldn't watch,

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:22.701
a guy notorious
for watching more TV

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:24.300
than is medically advisable,

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.434
and that's the president
of the United States.

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.501
Trump said this week,

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.801
he would not watch the testimony
because Democrats shouldn't

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.734
get to keep talking about
the Russia investigation.

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:35.901
-Mr. President --
-One question.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.968
-No, I'm not going to be
watching, probably.

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:39.133
Maybe I'll see
a little bit of it.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:42.033
I'm not going to be
watching Mueller,

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:44.534
because you can't take

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:46.334
all those bites
out of the apple.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.300
-Of course, Trump
thinks you can't take

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.033
all those bites out of the apple
because he's never taken

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.400
more than one bite
out of an apple,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.801
and that was a mistake.

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:57.634
[ As Trump ]
"This meatball is disgusting."

00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:59.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.767
[ Normal voice ] But it would
have been instructive for Trump

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:04.300
to watch because he clearly
has not read the report.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.901
I mean, it's over 400 pages.

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:07.033
There's no way Trump's ever

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.033
read anything that long
in his life.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.567
If he gets a fortune cookie
with his takeout,

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.033
he hands it to one of his aides.

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:16.200
[ As Trump ]
"Just give me the gist."

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.734
[ Normal voice ] In fact,
despite his obvious lie,

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:19.400
Trump almost certainly
was watching the hearings

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.601
because before
they even started,

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:23.467
he predictably lost his mind
on Twitter again.

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:25.968
All of these are
just from this morning.

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:29.300
-"So, Democrats and others can
illegally fabricate a crime,

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.667
try pinning it on
a very innocent president,

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.567
and when he fights back
against this illegal,

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:35.901
treasonous attack
on our country,

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.734
they call it obstruction --
wrong!

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:40.133
Why didn't Robert Mueller
investigate the investigators?"

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.234
-"Why didn't Robert Mueller

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.367
and his band
of 18 angry Democrats

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:46.267
spend any time investigating
crooked Hillary Clinton,

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:47.868
lying and leaking James Comey,

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:50.400
Lisa Page and her psycho lover
Peter Strzok,

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.734
Andy McCabe,
the beautiful Ohr family,

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:54.601
Fusion GPS, and many more,

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:57.133
including himself and Andrew W?"

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.834
"So, why didn't the highly-
conflicted Robert Mueller

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:02.767
investigate how and why
crooked Hillary Clinton

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:05.534
deleted and acid washed
33,000 e-mails

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:07.133
immediately
after getting a subpoena

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:08.701
from the United States Congress?

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:11.000
She must have great lawyers."

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.834
-"No collusion. No obstruction."

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:16.000
-"The greatest witch hunt
in U.S. history, by far."

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.234
-Dear God, his tweets
would make more sense

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:19.734
if they were scribbled on paper

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:25.000
and faxed to a newspaper
under the zodiac symbol.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.400
But at the very least,
today's hearings

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.567
might have been informative,

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:29.501
both for Trump
and for members of Congress

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:31.734
who have admitted they didn't
read the whole report.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.067
More than a dozen
members of Congress

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.334
readily admitted to Politico

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:36.000
that they, too,
have skipped around

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.300
rather than studying every one

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.901
of the special counsel
report's 448 pages.

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:41.133
That might explain

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:43.100
why some Democrats have
spent the last few months

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.133
trying to educate
their Republican colleagues

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:46.701
by reading sections
of the report

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:48.200
into the Congressional record,

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.434
including sections of the report
that include colorful language

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:53.801
which has given us fun clips
like these.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:58.067
-Page 78 of Volume 2
of the report says and I quote,

00:02:58.067 --> 00:02:59.701
"When Sessions
told the president

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:01.567
that a special counsel
had been appointed,

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:04.501
the president slumped back
in his chair and said,

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:07.234
'Oh, my God.
This is terrible.

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:09.334
This is the end
of my presidency.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.667
I'm [bleep].'"

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:15.234
-On Saturday, June 17, 2017,

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:17.267
the president called McGahn

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:20.868
and told him to have
the special counsel removed.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:25.334
That evening, McGahn called
both Priebus and Bannon

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:28.234
and told them that
he intended to resign.

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:31.167
Priebus recalled that McGahn
said that the president

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:35.801
had asked him to,
"Do crazy [bleep]."

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:37.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.534
-It is both great and weird

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:43.234
to hear a curse word
come out of Elizabeth Warren.

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:48.100
It's like watching a nun
take a hit off a joint.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.801
What they were reading
into the record

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.167
were details from the report

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:53.167
on Trump's various attempts
to obstruct justice,

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:55.200
including ordering his
former White House counsel

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.801
Don McGahn to fire Mueller.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:59.400
But Trump has repeatedly
insisted falsely

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.033
without offering any details

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:02.968
that Article 2
of the Constitution,

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:04.400
which is about
the executive branch,

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.033
gives him the power
to fire Mueller

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.133
and do whatever he wants.

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.234
He's repeated that argument
over and over,

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.400
including during
a rambling speech yesterday.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.801
-Article 2 allows me
to do whatever I want.

00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:16.000
Article 2 would have
allowed me to fire him.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.234
Nobody ever mentions Article 2.

00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:20.567
It gives me all of these rights

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:23.367
at a level that nobody
has ever seen before.

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:25.167
We don't even talk
about Article 2.

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:27.300
Then I have an Article 2

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.000
where I have the right to do
whatever I want as president,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.400
but I don't even
talk about that.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.501
-First, "I have an Article 2,"

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.868
is such a New York way
of saying it.

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.567
[ New York accent ] "It's not
jaywalking when I do it

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:44.667
because I got an Article 2
right here, buddy.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.968
Stop your honking."

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:48.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:50.801
[ Normal voice ] Also...

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:53.734
I like how he says,
"I don't talk about that,"

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:56.300
even though he constantly
talks about that.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.567
He's like a grandparent
who won't stop talking

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.100
about how you won't call.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.934
"I never hear from you,
not a phone call,

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.701
not an e-mail,
not even a card,

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:06.701
but still,
I don't complain."

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:10.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.701
Also Article 2 does not
give you the right

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:14.067
to do whatever you want.

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:15.200
If that's the case,

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.767
it would have been
a lot shorter.

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:21.868
This is why today's hearing
was so important.

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:24.634
The lawless president who openly
welcomed foreign interference

00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:26.200
and then tried
repeatedly to stop

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.033
the investigation
of that interference

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.300
thinks he can do
whatever he wants,

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.100
which is why we need a Congress

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.434
that will hold him accountable.

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:34.601
Now you heard the president
in his tweets today

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:35.968
and for the last few months,

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.167
he was totally and completely

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:38.501
exonerated
by the Mueller report,

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:40.567
and since Donald Trump
is known as a truthful guy,

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:41.834
I am sure once
the hearings began,

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:45.467
Robert Mueller confirmed exactly
what the president said.

00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:48.400
-The president has repeatedly
claimed that your report

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.868
found there was no obstruction

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:53.601
and that it completely
and totally exonerated him.

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:56.767
But that is not what
your report said, is it?

00:05:56.767 --> 00:05:58.968
-Correct. It is not
what the report said.

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:01.734
-So, the report did not conclude

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:04.000
that he did not commit
obstruction of justice?

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.767
Is that correct?

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:07.000
-That is correct.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.901
-And what about
total exoneration?

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:11.300
Did you actually totally
exonerate the president?

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.934
-No.
-What?

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:14.934
But Trump scream tweeted,

00:06:14.934 --> 00:06:16.901
"no collusion, no obstruction."

00:06:16.901 --> 00:06:18.400
It was in all caps,

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.400
and if it's in all caps,
you know it's true,

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.534
like when you get an e-mail
that says "free boner pills,"

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:27.033
you know it's legit.

00:06:27.033 --> 00:06:28.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:32.133
You're not gonna pay
for those boner pills.

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.834 --> 00:06:35.868
Right off the bat,
this was the key exchange.

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:37.501
We heard from the investigator,
himself,

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:39.267
that his report did not
exonerate the president.

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:42.467
In fact, there was at least
one very specific reason

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:44.734
Mueller couldn't just go ahead
and charge Trump with a crime,

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:46.200
and it's because of guidelines

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:50.000
from the Justice Department's
Office of Legal Counsel, or OLC,

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.133
that say a sitting President
cannot be indicted,

00:06:52.133 --> 00:06:53.434
which Mueller confirmed today.

00:06:53.434 --> 00:06:54.634
The chairman of
the Judiciary Committee

00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:56.601
Jerry Nadler also asked Mueller

00:06:56.601 --> 00:06:58.133
about his attempts
to interview Trump

00:06:58.133 --> 00:07:00.701
which Trump refused
and revealed how long

00:07:00.701 --> 00:07:03.300
Mueller had tried to get Trump
to sit down for an interview.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:05.567
-Did the president refuse
the request to be interviewed

00:07:05.567 --> 00:07:06.400
by you or your team?

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.267
-Yes.
-Yes?

00:07:08.267 --> 00:07:10.267
And is it true that you tried
for more than a year

00:07:10.267 --> 00:07:11.267
to secure an interview

00:07:11.267 --> 00:07:12.868
with the president?
-Yes.

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:14.200
-Well, you didn't go through
the proper channels.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.000
If you want Trump
to give you an answer,

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.434
you either need
to go to Fox News

00:07:17.434 --> 00:07:19.434
or send him a rambling tweet

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:21.801
that praises him in syntax
he's familiar with.

00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:24.434
"Mr. Very Innocent President,
sir, we would love for you

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:26.767
to sit down for a very
exonerating interview, sir,

00:07:26.767 --> 00:07:29.367
because you are the best
and most not guilty president,

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:33.968
with the most innocence, sir,
and everyone says so, sir."

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:37.734
And then...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:37.734 --> 00:07:40.200
And then after
the chairman's first questions

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.868
came time for the Republicans
to open up their questions

00:07:42.868 --> 00:07:44.300
with the ranking member
of the committee,

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:46.067
Doug Collins,
who warned Mueller

00:07:46.067 --> 00:07:48.334
that he would try
to speak slowly

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:50.934
and then immediately
rambled so quickly

00:07:50.934 --> 00:07:53.100
even Mueller
couldn't follow him.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:55.200
-I'll talk slowly.
It's said that I talk fast.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.467
I will talk slowly.

00:07:56.467 --> 00:07:58.133
Your report states that
your investigative team

00:07:58.133 --> 00:08:00.801
included 19 lawyers
and approximately 40 FBI agents,

00:08:00.801 --> 00:08:01.934
and analysts and accountants.

00:08:01.934 --> 00:08:03.634
Are those numbers accurate?

00:08:03.634 --> 00:08:05.167
-Could you repeat
that, please?

00:08:05.167 --> 00:08:08.100
-Is it also true that you
issued over 2,800 subpoenas,

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.934
executed nearly
500 search warrants,

00:08:09.934 --> 00:08:12.501
obtained more than 230 orders
for communication records

00:08:12.501 --> 00:08:13.968
and 50 pin registers.

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:16.334
-That went
a little fast for me.

00:08:16.334 --> 00:08:17.934
-Dude, are you
a member of Congress

00:08:17.934 --> 00:08:19.567
or an auctioneer?

00:08:19.567 --> 00:08:20.968
He didn't get
the answer he wanted,

00:08:20.968 --> 00:08:24.567
but he did sell three paintings
and a hog.

00:08:24.567 --> 00:08:26.200
Republicans also tried
to grill Mueller

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:27.434
by criticizing him

00:08:27.434 --> 00:08:28.834
for specifically
stating in his report

00:08:28.834 --> 00:08:30.234
that Trump had not
been exonerated,

00:08:30.234 --> 00:08:33.133
but as usual, they devolved
into partisan name calling,

00:08:33.133 --> 00:08:36.200
when Republican congressman
called Democrats socialists

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.100
and slammed Mueller
for how he handled

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.968
the allegations against Trump.

00:08:39.968 --> 00:08:42.968
-Americans need to know this,
as they listen to Democrats

00:08:42.968 --> 00:08:44.868
and socialists on
the other side of the aisle,

00:08:44.868 --> 00:08:46.834
I agree with the chairman
this morning

00:08:46.834 --> 00:08:49.000
when he said Donald Trump
is not above the law.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.734
He's not, but he damn sure

00:08:50.734 --> 00:08:52.000
shouldn't be below the law,

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.634
which is where Volume 2
of this report puts him.

00:08:54.634 --> 00:08:57.567
-No, I agree
because that isn't a thing.

00:08:57.567 --> 00:08:59.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:59.033 --> 00:09:00.968
Though if anyone
could be below the law,

00:09:00.968 --> 00:09:01.767
it's Donald Trump.

00:09:01.767 --> 00:09:03.200
Trump looks up at the law

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.834
the same way he looks up
at an eclipse.

00:09:05.834 --> 00:09:07.801
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.801 --> 00:09:10.767
"Below The Law" sounds
like a straight-to-video

00:09:10.767 --> 00:09:14.968
Steven Seagal movie
starring Donald Trump.

00:09:14.968 --> 00:09:17.501
Now, compare that tirade,

00:09:17.501 --> 00:09:20.200
to the straightforward questions
of some of the Democrats,

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:22.734
which produced matter-of-fact
yes-or-no answers.

00:09:22.734 --> 00:09:24.067
-An unsuccessful attempt

00:09:24.067 --> 00:09:25.601
to obstruct justice
is still a crime.

00:09:25.601 --> 00:09:26.601
Is that correct?

00:09:26.601 --> 00:09:27.968
-That is correct.

00:09:27.968 --> 00:09:29.501
-Does that mean
you have to investigate

00:09:29.501 --> 00:09:32.267
all of his conduct
to ascertain true motive?

00:09:32.267 --> 00:09:33.601
-No.

00:09:33.601 --> 00:09:37.767
-President Trump directed
White House Counsel Don McGahn

00:09:37.767 --> 00:09:39.000
to fire you.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.133
Isn't that correct?
-True.

00:09:41.133 --> 00:09:43.000
-Damn,
this hearing was flying so fast

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.968
it must have been impossible
for Trump to follow along.

00:09:44.968 --> 00:09:46.634
Remember, he's used to Fox News

00:09:46.634 --> 00:09:49.767
where his favorite hosts
speak slowly and loudly

00:09:49.767 --> 00:09:51.434
in words he can understand.

00:09:51.434 --> 00:09:57.701
-Paul Ryan needs to step down
as Speaker of the House.

00:09:57.701 --> 00:10:03.000
-See, nice and slow
in a New York accent.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.934
Jeanine Pirro...

00:10:06.934 --> 00:10:09.501
Jeanine Pirro is like
Dora the Explorer

00:10:09.501 --> 00:10:11.601
if she'd grown up
on Long Island.

00:10:11.601 --> 00:10:14.200
[ Long Island accent ]
"Can you help Boots find

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.701
the auto body shop?

00:10:16.701 --> 00:10:18.033
Good job.

00:10:18.033 --> 00:10:22.801
Molto bene!"

00:10:22.801 --> 00:10:24.033
[ Normal voice ]
This captured

00:10:24.033 --> 00:10:26.033
the fundamental weirdness
of the hearing.

00:10:26.033 --> 00:10:28.334
Mueller wants the report
to speak for itself,

00:10:28.334 --> 00:10:30.300
and that report is
incredibly damning on its own,

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:31.467
which is why Mueller

00:10:31.467 --> 00:10:33.534
often responded with
simple yes-or-no answers.

00:10:33.534 --> 00:10:36.033
In fact, so much of this hearing
consisted of the Democrats

00:10:36.033 --> 00:10:38.234
reading excerpts of the report
to Mueller

00:10:38.234 --> 00:10:40.367
and having Mueller
confirm he did, indeed,

00:10:40.367 --> 00:10:41.801
write those excerpts.

00:10:41.801 --> 00:10:44.334
-On Page 77 of Volume 2,

00:10:44.334 --> 00:10:45.834
your report also stated,

00:10:45.834 --> 00:10:48.734
"In addition,
some witnesses said

00:10:48.734 --> 00:10:50.901
that Trump privately
sought information

00:10:50.901 --> 00:10:54.100
about future
WikiLeaks releases."

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:55.567
Is that correct?
-Correct.

00:10:55.567 --> 00:10:58.567
-The president engaged
in efforts, and I quote,

00:10:58.567 --> 00:11:02.934
"To encourage witnesses
not to cooperate

00:11:02.934 --> 00:11:04.667
with the investigation."

00:11:04.667 --> 00:11:06.467
Is that right?
-That's correct.

00:11:06.467 --> 00:11:09.667
-Didn't the president say,
quote, and this is on page 116,

00:11:09.667 --> 00:11:11.000
"If he doesn't write a letter,

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.934
then maybe I'll have
to get rid of him."

00:11:13.934 --> 00:11:14.767
-Yes.

00:11:14.767 --> 00:11:16.067
-Yeah, he wrote it.

00:11:16.067 --> 00:11:17.901
That's why this whole thing
was so weird.

00:11:17.901 --> 00:11:20.100
He already wrote down
everything he knows.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:22.033
It's like if you called
in Ernest Hemingway

00:11:22.033 --> 00:11:24.200
to grill him about
one of his books.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.868
"Is it true that
one of the characters

00:11:25.868 --> 00:11:27.033
is an old man?"

00:11:27.033 --> 00:11:28.767
"Yes."

00:11:28.767 --> 00:11:30.767
"And he is, in fact,
on the sea?"

00:11:30.767 --> 00:11:33.434
"That is correct."

00:11:33.434 --> 00:11:35.868
Republicans, meanwhile, tried
to impugn Mueller's credibility

00:11:35.868 --> 00:11:39.000
Like when Congressman
Louie Gohmert bizarrely

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.434
asked Mueller if he was friends

00:11:40.434 --> 00:11:43.234
with former FBI director
James Comey who, of course,

00:11:43.234 --> 00:11:45.934
was fired by Trump after
Trump asked him for loyalty

00:11:45.934 --> 00:11:48.200
and told him to shut down
his investigation into

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.234
former national security adviser
Michael Flynn.

00:11:50.234 --> 00:11:53.501
-You and James Comey
have been good friends,

00:11:53.501 --> 00:11:55.901
were good friends,
for many years.

00:11:55.901 --> 00:11:58.133
Correct?
-We were business associates.

00:11:58.133 --> 00:12:00.234
We both started off in
the Justice Department --

00:12:00.234 --> 00:12:01.734
-You were good friends.

00:12:01.734 --> 00:12:03.567
You can work together
and not be friends,

00:12:03.567 --> 00:12:06.367
But you and Comey were friends.
-We were friends.

00:12:06.367 --> 00:12:08.501
-Gohmert might just be jealous
that, unlike him,

00:12:08.501 --> 00:12:10.367
people have friends.

00:12:10.367 --> 00:12:12.067
"And this friend of yours,

00:12:12.067 --> 00:12:13.834
he's someone you can
have lunch with,

00:12:13.834 --> 00:12:16.567
maybe catch a ball game,

00:12:16.567 --> 00:12:18.000
and when you're going
through a rough patch

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:21.667
in your personal life,
he's there to lend an ear?

00:12:21.667 --> 00:12:23.267
Maybe your family and his family

00:12:23.267 --> 00:12:24.767
take a vacation together
once in a while?

00:12:24.767 --> 00:12:28.167
Well, that must be
very nice for you.

00:12:28.167 --> 00:12:30.467
Mr. Mueller, I have
one question for you.

00:12:30.467 --> 00:12:32.267
Will you be my friend?"

00:12:32.267 --> 00:12:33.701
-No.

00:12:33.701 --> 00:12:36.200
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:37.400
-And then Gohmert went off

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:40.501
on an unhinged rant
that went on for so long

00:12:40.501 --> 00:12:42.567
he eventually got cut off
by the chairman of the committee

00:12:42.567 --> 00:12:44.834
which led to a very curt
response from Mueller.

00:12:44.834 --> 00:12:46.834
-If somebody knows

00:12:46.834 --> 00:12:49.467
they did not conspire

00:12:49.467 --> 00:12:51.400
with anybody from Russia

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:53.434
to effect the election,

00:12:53.434 --> 00:12:56.834
and they see the big
Justice Department

00:12:56.834 --> 00:12:59.667
with people that
hate that person

00:12:59.667 --> 00:13:01.267
coming after them,

00:13:01.267 --> 00:13:04.033
and then
a special counsel appointed

00:13:04.033 --> 00:13:07.200
who hires dozens or more people

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:09.167
that hate that person,

00:13:09.167 --> 00:13:12.267
and he knows he's innocent,

00:13:12.267 --> 00:13:15.334
he's not corruptly acting

00:13:15.334 --> 00:13:18.100
in order to see
that justice is done.

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:21.767
What he's doing is not
obstructing justice.

00:13:21.767 --> 00:13:24.701
He is pursuing justice
and the fact that you...

00:13:24.701 --> 00:13:26.267
-Gentleman's time --
-...ran it out two years

00:13:26.267 --> 00:13:29.367
means you perpetuated injustice.
-The gentleman's time --

00:13:29.367 --> 00:13:32.033
-I take -- I take your question.
-Gentleman's time is expired.

00:13:32.033 --> 00:13:34.334
-The witness may
answer the question.

00:13:34.334 --> 00:13:36.834
-I take your question.

00:13:36.834 --> 00:13:38.968
[ Light laughter ]

00:13:38.968 --> 00:13:40.934
-Now, apparently

00:13:40.934 --> 00:13:42.334
"I take your question"

00:13:42.334 --> 00:13:44.267
is a pretty standard
legal response,

00:13:44.267 --> 00:13:48.968
but it sounded like some
Dowager-Countess-level shade.

00:13:48.968 --> 00:13:50.534
"I take your question.

00:13:50.534 --> 00:13:53.801
Now, if you don't mind,
do [bleep] right off."

00:13:53.801 --> 00:13:55.100
[ Laughter ]

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.100
In particular, Republicans
seem focused on the fact

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.234
that Mueller listed
possible instances

00:14:00.234 --> 00:14:01.400
of obstruction of justice

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.267
and said he cannot
exonerate the president.

00:14:03.267 --> 00:14:06.100
Republicans basically argued
that it was unfair for Mueller

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:07.901
to put that information
in the report

00:14:07.901 --> 00:14:09.901
if he could not
indict the president,

00:14:09.901 --> 00:14:11.767
even though the rule
specifically said

00:14:11.767 --> 00:14:14.601
he wasn't allowed
to indict the president.

00:14:14.601 --> 00:14:16.868
But then one Republican
congressman accidentally

00:14:16.868 --> 00:14:19.367
got Mueller to offer
an extremely revealing answer

00:14:19.367 --> 00:14:20.567
on whether Trump could ever be

00:14:20.567 --> 00:14:22.033
charged with a crime
in the future.

00:14:22.033 --> 00:14:26.167
-Was there sufficient evidence
to convict President Trump

00:14:26.167 --> 00:14:29.200
or anyone else with
obstruction of justice?

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.334
-Uh, we did not make
that calculation.

00:14:31.334 --> 00:14:33.167
-How could you not have
made the calculation?

00:14:33.167 --> 00:14:34.834
-Because the OLC Opinion --

00:14:34.834 --> 00:14:37.267
the OLC opinion,
Office of Legal Counsel,

00:14:37.267 --> 00:14:40.267
indicates that we cannot
indict a sitting president.

00:14:40.267 --> 00:14:42.300
-Okay, but the --

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:45.334
Could you charge the president
with a crime

00:14:45.334 --> 00:14:47.667
after he left office?
-Yes.

00:14:47.667 --> 00:14:49.067
-You believe that
he committed --

00:14:49.067 --> 00:14:50.767
You could charge the president
of the United States

00:14:50.767 --> 00:14:52.834
with obstruction of justice
after he left office?

00:14:52.834 --> 00:14:53.667
-Yes.

00:14:53.667 --> 00:14:56.801
-Oh, those were very fast yeses.

00:14:56.801 --> 00:14:58.801
"And would you like to be there
the day he's arrested?"

00:14:58.801 --> 00:15:01.033
"Yes."

00:15:01.033 --> 00:15:03.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
That guy was a Republican.

00:15:03.334 --> 00:15:06.634
He was a Republican,

00:15:06.634 --> 00:15:08.567
who accidentally
got Robert Mueller

00:15:08.567 --> 00:15:11.000
to say on national television
that after Trump leaves office,

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:11.934
he can be charged with a crime.

00:15:11.934 --> 00:15:13.234
You know when Trump heard that,

00:15:13.234 --> 00:15:15.100
he started pushing the sofa
in front of the door.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:18.000
[ As Trump ]
"You'll never take me alive."

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.634
[ Normal voice ] The bottom line
from today's hearings

00:15:19.634 --> 00:15:20.968
is the same as it's always been.

00:15:20.968 --> 00:15:23.200
We just got to see it played out
live on TV.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:25.234
Russia interfered in
the election to help trump.

00:15:25.234 --> 00:15:27.000
Trump welcomed and encouraged
that help,

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.901
and then he almost certainly
committed crimes

00:15:28.901 --> 00:15:31.133
to obstruct the investigation
of that help.

00:15:31.133 --> 00:15:32.934
Mueller couldn't indict Trump

00:15:32.934 --> 00:15:34.300
so the only remedy
is impeachment.

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:35.567
It's up to Congress now.

00:15:35.567 --> 00:15:36.934
They're the only ones
who can hold the president

00:15:36.934 --> 00:15:38.067
accountable for his...

00:15:38.067 --> 00:15:40.167
-Crazy [bleep].
[ Laughter ]

00:15:40.167 --> 00:15:41.667
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:41.667 --> 00:15:43.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

